            headline: "source-intent integration core — SCM-compatible, not SCM-shaped",
            brief: "Native UX is edit → submit → Landed. Primary outcomes are Landed; Choice required, one genuine domain-language preference with previews and stored continuation; or Could not land, a plain terminal refusal after every permitted machine-owned continuation is exhausted. Only the first two are semantic handoffs. Normal users never operate upstream topology or read proof vocabulary. Internally, claim-indexed evidence feeds a bounded kernel; semantic, admission, commit/read-back, and projection stay separate. Compatibility realizations are downstream and vendor-neutral to the kernel.",
            displaced_cost: "Agent-scale integration judgment and freshness waste: explicit stress profile = 50 agents/developer, 10 proposals in one modeled region, 30-minute CI; every invalidated green receipt repeats affected validation and delays admission, while a silent wrong automatic result spends recovery time later at interest.",
