            brief: "After the managed Git path is trusted, selected coding agents submit authenticated authored transformations and explicit contracts while the Git target remains source authority. Occurrence identity, parent, reads/relies, modifies/frame, ensures/guarantees, dependencies, atomicity, and continuation survive as additional evidence; ordinary commits and editors remain a lower-fidelity compatible path.",
