            brief: "A4 is an explicit per-target authority transition after successful managed Git landing and native-proposal evidence, never the default architecture. The native state remains exportable as ordinary Git. Storage has N realizations and an explicit PackingPolicy; semantic unit/group grain is independent of physical object grain and UnpackedNodeGrain is never the default. Serving rides the compute fabric only after tenant, visibility, restore, exit, and incident contracts are proven.",
