fn section_3() -> RoadmapSection {
  RoadmapSection {
    title: "3. The floor — audit what we have (does it actually do what it claims?)",
    elements: [
      section_prose(content: "Both pillars ride the CI floor: tree-wide marker-driven witness discovery · compile-clean gate · generated-artifact drift gates (this document is one) · `regen --verify` (#5873) · doc-graph reachability · emit-determinism (#5941) · the interim self-host comparison (#6009). Those stand. The floor's *expansion* lanes (testgen, wiring-liveness, complexity gates, lens meta-walls) are shelved — a new wall must displace a measured cost on a pillar path to un-shelve (the **enforcement-intent gate** below is the first such un-shelve, 2026-07-02: displaced cost = the operator's repeated manual *what-is-enforced-by-what-lens-over-what-corpus* join, plus CI-killing quadratics and repeated dual-representation/anemia rediscovery)."),
      section_prose(content: "**Audit directive (operator, 2026-07-01): thoroughly audit what we have and what it actually does.** For each load-bearing mechanism, prove **by execution** that it does what it claims, with a **discriminating perturb** that goes RED when the behavior is wrong — a typecheck or a grep is not a consumer (DESIGN §5), and a wired gate can still be vacuous. A mechanism claim without a red-control is *unverified*, whatever its docs say. The reset's own mapping found the pattern live: the committed converge shell is spec-without-execution (§2), the fixpoint gate self-declares interim (2-of-92 files), cargo-green is an ignored test. Highest-stakes mechanisms first:"),
      section_group(
        label: "Audit — green by execution, red by perturbation",
        nodes: [
          ticket_row(id: "3-audit-affected-set", done: true, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "affected-set lens — discharged by a standing mechanism",
            brief: "(a) soundness = the 4-hourly falsifier runs the corpus cold with predictions recorded, counted divergence is the RED — and it discriminated live (the 07-16..07-21 red period was real roster gaps, healed #7083; alert loudness #7022); (b) effectiveness = discovery-flip receipt 8→~1,721 witnesses/PR + regen affected-set ~4m45s/PR (#6732) + compile-clean closure scoping (#6658); (c) fail-closed = #6525 ReadsLiveTree never-skip and a provenance gap REFUSES, never widens.",
            displaced_cost: "",
            current_state: "the original run-all wording predates the §5 absorbing-fallback ruling — corrected here",
            first_slice: "",
            red_control: "",
            out_of_scope: "",
            handback: "",
            updates: [
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-23", note: "audit discharge dated" },
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-25", note: "migrated to ticket form (W2-bulk tranche 14)" },
            ],
            authored_on: "",
            last_verified_on: "2026-07-23",
          }),
          sign(rn: owned(rn: with_plan(rn: authored_wi(id: "3-audit-gate-inventory", done: true, content: "**mechanism inventory with red-controls** — census every wired gate/lens/cache (floor-plan roster + `commit_workflow`): what it claims · its discriminating RED witness · its last execution receipt. Anything without a red-control gets one or gets demoted/deleted. The inert-lens backstop (#5433) covers *wiring*; this covers *claim-vs-behavior*.", intricacy: IntricacyMedium, volume: VolumeLarge, repo: "gunbc"), path: "docs/plans/mechanism-inventory-red-controls.md"), owner: "dispatched 2026-07-01 · adhoc-c67edbed-916"), s: signed(by: "operator", works: true, scope_equivalent: true, as_expected: true)),
          ticket_row(id: "3-audit-cache-honesty", done: false, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "cache honesty re-receipt",
            brief: "Re-run the warm==cold purity oracle against CURRENT main (616/616 was pre-reset), and close the sccache exit-0-no-binary class; a cache that lies is worse than no cache.",
            displaced_cost: "",
            current_state: "",
            first_slice: "",
            red_control: "",
            out_of_scope: "",
            handback: "",
            updates: [
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-25", note: "migrated to ticket form (W2-bulk tranche 14)" },
            ],
            authored_on: "",
            last_verified_on: "",
          }),
          ticket_wi(id: "3-audit-artifact-freshness", done: false, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "artifact-freshness gate",
            brief: "We half-have one: the per-PR drift gate proves committed==emitted for the PR's OWN tree, but drift still LANDED on main (.gitignore stale vs its authority since #6097; found and healed by #6110/#6111) because admission never re-validates against CURRENT main — green-on-branch is not green-on-main. The closing mechanism is the §2 merge-admission freshness block (HELD); this item is its receipt pair.",
            displaced_cost: "drift landing on main through stale-base greens",
            current_state: "",
            first_slice: "(a) reproduce the landed-drift path as a RED witness, (b) confirm the freshness block refuses it once un-HELD",
            red_control: "",
            out_of_scope: "",
            handback: "",
            updates: [
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-25", note: "migrated to ticket form (W2-bulk tranche 14); the operator ask preserved: we need a freshness gate, if we don't already have one" },
            ],
            authored_on: "",
            last_verified_on: "",
          }, intricacy: IntricacyMedium, volume: VolumeSmall, repo: "gunbc"),
          superseded(id: "3-audit-gate-disagreement", by: "namespace-only resolution lane (operator-signed 2026-07-06) — docs/plans/namespace-resolution-design.md", content: "**one tree, one verdict** — the concrete forks dissolved: #6950 gate loader runs both closures (the exact gate-green/floor-red fork), #6935 reference_resolution_facts builtin de-forked the module-graph host; the systemic one-resolution-authority ask IS the namespace lane. Residual to carry: the gate-equivalent local invocation is still flag-sensitive (--dependency-pool-index primary-precedence)."),
          ticket_row(id: "3-enforcement-intent", done: false, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "enforcement intent + model-quality walls",
            brief: "Substantially LANDED, re-based 2026-07-23: carrier family src/v2/lens/enforcement/ (standing_intent, contract, gate, receipts) + enforcement_live.dag on main; children A+B via #6756 (Question-0 lens-module gate, StandingIntent fail-closed); C carrier standing_intent_complexity_repo_wide exists; D's object rule effectively landed (#6527 accumulator-copy as required root-grain compile lens + #6540); E first consumer merged (model_anemia lens). [design](docs/plans/enforcement-intent-design.md)",
            displaced_cost: "",
            current_state: "post-landing churn: #7070 de-enrolled lens_module_gate from the compile door (corpus-grain invariant, tree-grain roster)",
            first_slice: "fold that churn in, finish the C receipts, close the DESIGN open thread",
            red_control: "",
            out_of_scope: "",
            handback: "",
            updates: [
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-23", note: "re-based; landed inventory dated" },
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-25", note: "migrated to ticket form (W2-bulk tranche 14). Queue note recorded: the state-response census (composition slice 1) is a third consumer idling on this machinery" },
            ],
