            last_verified_on: "2026-07-23",
          }),
        ],
        edges: [],
      ),
      section_group(
        label: "Cost / risk / benefit — the floor's unmodeled optimization",
        nodes: [
          ticket_pp(id: "3-cost-risk-benefit", done: false, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "model cost/risk/benefit — what we actually run is one optimization, not a pile of policies",
            brief: "Affected-set, wet/dry, receipt/long, ReadsLiveTree never-skip, and the test-kind names are all UNMODELED PROXIES for argmax(benefit − cost) under a budget — hand-tuned stand-ins that exist because the axes were never first-class. Root anemia: test fn bakes in cost ≈ 0 run-always, which is false. The fail-closed invariant: you may trade fidelity for cost (mocks, skips, deferrals), but the traded-away risk must stay OBSERVABLE on a cadence — deferred-and-detected, never silent. This inverts wet-is-sacred: wet is a highest-cost fidelity point, usually not worth it.",
            displaced_cost: "the hand-tuned policy pile (mostly astrology)",
            current_state: "landed as approximation in #6506 (Stages 0–2): hermetic-by-default floor, a flat hand-set 5s per-witness budget (fail-closed EvalBudgetExceeded), the test/claim/long cadence — right shape, interim stand-ins. Missing, highlighted not papered over: no per-effect cost model; the budget flat, not graph-derived nor wall-clock-allocated; benefit unmodeled except the §5 lower bound (no discriminating red ⟹ ~0 gate-value ⟹ drop — a pure demo) and observed red-frequency. Bootstrappable now: the floor already measures wall_nanos/cgroup-peak per claim — cost = measured receipt now, graph-derived later",
            first_slice: "cost first (from what is measurable now) with budget-aware admission and counted typed deferrals — never silent skip — then benefit (the §5 lower bound + red-frequency, declared interim), then the proxies reconcile onto the axes",
            red_control: "",
            out_of_scope: "",
            handback: "",
            updates: [
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-12", note: "operator working session — the capture this ticket decomposes" },
              TicketUpdate { on: "2026-07-25", note: "migrated to ticket form (W2-bulk tranche 14)" },
            ],
            authored_on: "2026-07-12",
            last_verified_on: "",
          }, carriers: [ptr(label: "cost/risk/benefit model", path: "docs/plans/cost-risk-benefit-floor-model.md")]),
