          ticket_wi(id: "ts-dispatch-latch", done: false, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "the dispatch control latches from observed Live, and release stays fail-closed",
            brief: "Once the Live lamp is authoritative, the dispatch control may consume it as a latch: raised dispatches; pressed releases only through R5. The control never infers Live from its last click. Every start, stop, or refusal re-observes before changing the latch. A refused teardown leaves it pressed because teardown did not happen; an unknowable read renders refused, never off. Release must remain explicit: either a two-step gesture or the existing stop chip.",
            displaced_cost: "the live button currently looks settled but still dispatches again, while Stop is a separate dynamically-created control; the action and its observed state disagree",
