          authored(id: "ts-intake-discipline", done: false, content: "**until the actuator lands, this sheet is the intake queue** — new work enters as a row here or as a sized lane node with an Accept line, never ad hoc mid-session; dispatch top-down by the numbering; a session that discovers work files a row instead of chasing it."),
          ticket_row(id: "ts-dispatch-lifecycle", done: false, t: TicketFields {
            headline: "each dispatched item is a real workflow, not a single hop",
            brief: "Required artifacts and observations: MODEL first (concept/authority delta + acceptance claims), BRIEF generated from row + model, IMPLEMENT attempts, ANTAGONISTIC REVIEW against the brief, LANDED PR evidence, and operator ACCEPTANCE. This list is a discipline and may be ordered for presentation; the machine stores independent facts, not one stage. MERGE IS NOT DONE: a merge certifies a diff landed, while only the separate acceptance verdict closes the work item.",
            displaced_cost: "the #7087 pattern: worker hits gaps, does half, flags honestly, PR merges — and the item silently reads done; the absorbing fallback at the management layer",
